{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>You remembered</b> — This verse is a sign for a year of drought that was in Zion, and the enemy thought to come against Zion to besiege it, and HaShem remembered His land, which is the land of Israel." "Some say: <b>תשוקקיה</b> — like <b>ותשקיה</b>, and this is not correct. And as for 'and the soul longs,' it is only like: <b>וירם תולעים ויבאש</b> and already <b>ובאש</b>, and thus there are many." "Thus it is '<b>You remembered the earth</b>' — and You have already made it channel with water, and on account of this he mentioned 'remembered.'" "<b>You saturated</b> — the tav is like in <b>ושבת לנשיא</b>, and the adjective is deficient, like the sense of <b>דברה רבה</b>." "<b>They are enriched</b> — it should have had a chirik under the shin if the word is from the intensive binyan, and if from the light binyan the verb would be transitive, like <b>יעשר</b>, which is shin — one will find thus for all three binyanim." "<b>Channel</b> — joined to 'the rain,' and the mem of <b>דגנם</b> returns to 'You remembered the earth.'" "<b>For so You prepare it</b> — returns to the earth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:51.036773002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}